{
  "hexparty": {
    "configuration": {
      "title": "Hexparty Configs",
      "section.hexparty.common.toml": {
        "": "Hexparty Configs",
        "title": "Hexparty Configs"
      }
    },
    "tooltip": {
      http_response: "HTTPResponse \"%s\""
    },
    "entry": {
      "http_spells": "HexParty"
    },
    "page": {
      "http_spells": {
        "entry": "These patterns seem to hint at a world outside of this one. Upon casting they seem to reach out to this other world and, after a bit of time send back information from it. Though this world seems insubstantial, I can still use it to store information or even hexes. Most take a $(thing)path$() which is a string formatted like this \"users/me/myhex\" and return a Response Iota.",
        "explanation": "To use the following pattern, one needs a $(thing)Path$() and $(br)optionally, one may also include a $(thing)method$() as a string, $(thing)headers$() as a list of key-value string pairs ([key, value,...]), and a $(thing)body$() as a string.$(br)Supported $(thing)Methods$(): GET,POST,PUT,DELETE,HEAD,OPTIONS,PATCH,TRACE$(br2)I believe $(l:https://github.com/9001/copyparty/blob/hovudstraum/docs/devnotes.md#http-api)this$() reference may be useful in understanding this pattern more",
        "request": "$(br)This seems to be a more complex but flexible verson of $(thing)Get CopyParty$(). Sends a request to the given $(thing)Path$(). Optionally, the $(thing)method$() used, $(thing)headers$() attached, and the $(thing)body$() of data sent with it may also be specified.",
        "get_response": "Given a Response iota, attempt to parse the results. Will Mishap if too early or an error is thrown.",
        "get_copyparty": "Given a path and a password, attempts to make a request to the hexparty path given. You *can* do this with the request pattern, but it is significantly easier to do it this way.",
        "set_copyparty": "Given a path, iotas, and password, attempts to store the iotas at that hexparty path. You *can* do this with the Request pattern, but it is significantly better to do it this way.",
        "iota_from_response": "Given a Response attempted to extract a pattern list, using something called $(thing)\"JSON\"$() as an intermediary. (Ducky Peripherals' mappings)",
        "get_code": "Given a response iota returns a status code that indicates whether the information has been retrieved successfully or not. 200 for success, -1 for in progress, and 404 for information not found.",

      }
    }
  },
  hexcasting: {
    mishap: {
